.TH "oc\-sessions" "1" "November 2026" "oc\-sessions" "General Commands Manual"
.SS NAME
oc\-sessions \[em] list recent opencode sessions with ready\-to\-run
launch commands
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]oc\-sessions\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] [\f[I]COUNT\f[R]]
.SS DESCRIPTION
\f[B]oc\-sessions\f[R] lists your recent \f[I]opencode\f[R] sessions,
newest first, together with the
\f[CR]cd ... && opencode \-\-session=...\f[R] command needed to reopen
each one.
Sessions are persisted by opencode in an SQLite database
(\f[CR]\[ti]/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db\f[R]), so the listing
works even after a reboot or a lost terminal.
.PP
Note: you must \f[CR]cd\f[R] into a session\[cq]s directory before
launching, because opencode resolves sessions per project directory.
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-a\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-all\f[R]
Include child/subagent sessions (they are hidden by default).
.TP
\f[CR]\-f\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-format\f[R] \f[I]FORMAT\f[R]
Output format: \f[CR]pretty\f[R], \f[CR]tsv\f[R], \f[CR]json\f[R], or
\f[CR]cmd\f[R] (see FORMATS).
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Show help.
.TP
\f[I]COUNT\f[R]
Number of sessions to list (default 10).
.SS FORMATS
.TP
\f[CR]pretty\f[R]
Human\-readable listing with launch commands (default).
.TP
\f[CR]tsv\f[R]
One row per session, \f[CR]|\f[R]\-separated:
\f[CR]updated|title|id|directory\f[R].
.TP
\f[CR]json\f[R]
JSON array of \f[CR]{updated, title, id, directory}\f[R] objects.
.TP
\f[CR]cmd\f[R]
Only the \f[CR]cd <dir> && opencode \-\-session=<id>\f[R] launch lines,
one per session \[em] convenient for scripting.
.SS ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[CR]OPENCODE_DB\f[R]
Path to the opencode SQLite database (default:
\f[CR]\[ti]/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db\f[R]).
.SS EXAMPLES
List the 10 most recent sessions:
.IP
.EX
oc\-sessions
.EE
.PP
Get the ID of the most recent session:
.IP
.EX
oc\-sessions \-f json 1 | jq \-r \[aq].[0].id\[aq]
.EE
.PP
Prepare the launch commands for the last 5 sessions:
.IP
.EX
oc\-sessions \-f cmd 5
.EE
.PP
Find sessions belonging to one project:
.IP
.EX
oc\-sessions \-f tsv 50 | grep \-i myproject | cut \-d\[aq]|\[aq] \-f3
.EE
.SS INSTALL
Symlink the script into a directory on your \f[CR]PATH\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
ln \-s \[ti]/Code/OpenCodeRecentSessions/oc\-sessions \[ti]/.local/bin/oc\-sessions
.EE
.PP
Install this man page:
.IP
.EX
mkdir \-p \[ti]/.local/share/man/man1
cp oc\-sessions.1 \[ti]/.local/share/man/man1/
.EE
